:: Basement - public punishment [bg-settlement]
<h1 class="ptitle">SETTLEMENT</h1>
<br />

<<addhours 2>>
<<energy -20>>

/* Pick from all available adult slaves */
<<set _allSlaveIds = []>>
<<set _availF = setup.getAvailablePersons18yo($slaves)[0] ?? []>>
<<set _availM = setup.getAvailablePersons18yo($slaves)[1] ?? []>>
<<set _allSlaveIds = _availF.concat(_availM)>>

<<set _punishedIds = []>>
<<set _count = Math.min(_allSlaveIds.length, either(2, 2, 3))>>
<<for _pi to 0; _pi lt _count; _pi++>>
    <<set _pick = setup.getRandomElement(_allSlaveIds.filter(id => !_punishedIds.includes(id)))>>
    <<if typeof _pick !== 'undefined'>>
        <<run _punishedIds.push(_pick)>>
    <</if>>
<</for>>
<<set _p1 = $slaves[_punishedIds[0]] ?? null>>
<<set _p2 = $slaves[_punishedIds[1]] ?? null>>
<<set _p3 = $slaves[_punishedIds[2]] ?? null>>

/* Determine image variant based on majority gender */
<<set _maleCount = _punishedIds.filter(id => $slaves[id]?.gender === 1 || $slaves[id]?.gender === 3).length>>
<<set _imgVariant = _maleCount > _punishedIds.length / 2 ? 'm' : 'f'>>

<<set _mistressIds = setup.getPersonsForLocation($guests, 'mistress')>>
<<set _hasMistress = _mistressIds.length > 0>>
<<set _mistress = _hasMistress ? $guests[_mistressIds[0]] : null>>

<!-- #### public_punishment_f.jpg | Post-apocalyptic settlement square, crowd of survivors watching a public punishment of two women, man standing in the center, bright midday light, grim atmosphere --ar 5:3 --p -->
<!-- #### public_punishment_m.jpg | Post-apocalyptic settlement square, crowd of survivors watching a public punishment of two men kneeling, authoritative man standing over them, harsh daylight --ar 5:3 --p -->
<center>
    <<image `'places/basement/public_punishment_' + _imgVariant + '.jpg'`>>
</center>
<br />

You had them brought up from the basement and marched out into the square. No announcement, no explanation. Word spread on its own — the way it always did here — and by the time you reached the centre, people had already stopped what they were doing.
<br /><br />

Settlers lined the edges. Everyone could see.
<br /><br />

<<if _hasMistress>>
    <<sayNpc _mistress>>
        Stay where you are. All of you. Watch.
    <</sayNpc>>
    <br />
    <<=setup.displayName(_mistress)>> stepped out ahead of the group, ensuring no one looked away.
<<else>>
    You pointed at <<=_p1 ? setup.displayName(_p1) : 'one of them'>> first. Then <<=_p2 ? setup.displayName(_p2) : 'another'>>.
    The square went quiet.
<</if>>
<br /><br />

<<linkreplace 'Begin the punishment'>>

    <!-- #### punishment_kneel_f.jpg | Two women kneeling in a post-apocalyptic settlement square in broad daylight, crowd watching silently, tense atmosphere --ar 5:3 --p -->
    <!-- #### punishment_kneel_m.jpg | Two men forced to kneel in a post-apocalyptic settlement square, crowd of onlookers surrounding them, daylight, tense grim atmosphere --ar 5:3 --p -->
    <center>
        <<image `'places/basement/punishment_kneel_' + _imgVariant + '.jpg'`>>
    </center>
    <br />

    <<if _p1>>
        <<=setup.displayName(_p1)>> was brought forward first — made to kneel in the open, in plain sight, in front of everyone they'd spent months living beside. No explanation. No warning. Just the flat fact of it.
    <</if>>
    <<if _p2>>
        <<=setup.displayName(_p2)>> followed, pulled up beside <<=_p1 ? setup.pronounceWho(_p1) : 'them'>> and forced into the same position.
    <</if>>
    <<if _p3>>
        <<=setup.displayName(_p3)>> came on <<=_p3 ? setup.pronounceWhos(_p3) : 'their'>> own when you looked at <<=_p3 ? setup.pronounceWho(_p3) : 'them'>>.
    <</if>>
    <br /><br />

    The square was completely still. No one looked away.
    <br /><br />

    You walked a slow circle around them. In public, out in the open, the silence carried further.
    <br /><br />

    <<linkreplace 'Continue'>>

        <!-- #### punishment_action_f.jpg | Man publicly punishing a kneeling woman in a post-apocalyptic settlement square, crowd watching in silence, harsh daylight --ar 5:3 --p -->
        <!-- #### punishment_action_m.jpg | Man publicly punishing a kneeling man in a post-apocalyptic settlement square, crowd of silent onlookers, harsh daylight --ar 5:3 --p -->
        <center>
            <<image `'places/basement/punishment_action_' + _imgVariant + '.jpg'`>>
        </center>
        <br />

        The punishment was methodical and unhurried. Straps. Hands. Whatever was at hand. The sound of it carried across the square in the open air — and the square made no sound back.
        <br /><br />

        <<if _p1>>
            <<if (_p1.traits ?? []).includes('masochist')>>
                <<=setup.displayName(_p1)>> made a noise that wasn't quite pain. Which was its own kind of message to everyone watching.
            <<else>>
                <<=setup.displayName(_p1)>> didn't cry out until the third stroke. By the fifth <<=setup.pronounceWhat(_p1)>> had gone somewhere else entirely.
            <</if>>
        <</if>>
        <<if _p2>>
            <<if (_p2.traits ?? []).includes('masochist')>>
                <<=setup.displayName(_p2)>> met your eyes at one point. There was something complicated in them.
            <<else>>
                <<=setup.displayName(_p2)>> kept <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_p2)>> head down and didn't fight it.
            <</if>>
        <</if>>
        <br /><br />

        Around the square, the watchers stood rigid. Some had gone pale. A few couldn't look — though they didn't dare turn away either.
        <br /><br />

        <<linkreplace 'Make them submit'>>

            <<if _hasMistress>>
                <<sayNpc _mistress>>
                    Say it. Loud enough for everyone to hear.
                <</sayNpc>>
                <br />
            <</if>>

            <<if _p1>>
                <<=setup.displayName(_p1)>> said it. Loud enough. The words came out small and flat — submission stripped of anything except compliance.
                <br /><br />
            <</if>>
            <<if _p2>>
                <<=setup.displayName(_p2)>> followed. <<if (_p2.traits ?? []).includes('masochist')>>Said it with something almost like relief.<br /><<else>>Said it quietly and didn't raise <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_p2)>> head.<br /><</if>>
            <</if>>
            <<if _p3>>
                <<=setup.displayName(_p3)>> didn't need to be asked twice.
                <br />
            <</if>>
            <br />

            You looked around the square once. Nobody moved.
            <br /><br />

            That was the point. Not the pain. Not the words. The stillness after — and the fact that everyone had seen it.
            <br /><br />

            /* Apply stat changes to punished slaves */
            <<for _pi, _pid range _punishedIds>>
                <<set _ps = $slaves[_pid]>>
                <<if _ps>>
                    <<set _ps.sub = Math.min((_ps.sub ?? 0) + 20, 100)>>
                    <<if (_ps.traits ?? []).includes('masochist')>>
                        <<set _ps.happy = Math.min((_ps.happy ?? 0) + 5, 100)>>
                    <<else>>
                        <<set _ps.happy = Math.max((_ps.happy ?? 0) - 10, -100)>>
                    <</if>>
                <</if>>
            <</for>>

            /* All other slaves watching: submission +10 */
            <<for _si, _slave range $slaves>>
                <<if !_punishedIds.includes(_si) && setup.getAge(_slave) >= 18>>
                    <<set $slaves[_si].sub = Math.min(($slaves[_si].sub ?? 0) + 10, 100)>>
                <</if>>
            <</for>>

            /* Voluntary guests in basement witness it: submission +5 */
            <<for _gi, _guest range $guests>>
                <<if (_guest.basementVoluntary ?? false) && setup.getAge(_guest) >= 18>>
                    <<set $guests[_gi].sub = Math.min(($guests[_gi].sub ?? 0) + 5, 100)>>
                <</if>>
            <</for>>

            <strong>
                <<if _p1>><<=setup.displayName(_p1)>>: Sub +20<<if (_p1.traits ?? []).includes('masochist')>>, Happy +5<<else>>, Happy −10<</if>><br /><</if>>
                <<if _p2>><<=setup.displayName(_p2)>>: Sub +20<<if (_p2.traits ?? []).includes('masochist')>>, Happy +5<<else>>, Happy −10<</if>><br /><</if>>
                <<if _p3>><<=setup.displayName(_p3)>>: Sub +20<<if (_p3.traits ?? []).includes('masochist')>>, Happy +5<<else>>, Happy −10<</if>><br /><</if>>
                All other slaves: Sub +10<br />
                <<if ($guests.some(g => g.basementVoluntary))>>Watching guests: Sub +5<br /><</if>>
            </strong>
            <br />

            <<link 'Return'>>
                <<goto 'Wood cabin'>>
            <</link>>

        <</linkreplace>>
    <</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
